Third-party material

The files src/ngsl.txt and src/nawl.txt, and the copies of them built into
index.html, are the New General Service List (version 1.2) and the New Academic
Word List (version 1.2) by Charles Browne, Brent Culligan and Joseph Phillips
(https://www.newgeneralservicelist.com/). They are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0), not
under the MIT licence above.

The files in model/ are used only by the optional meaning model and keep their
own licences: the all-MiniLM-L6-v2 sentence-embedding model (ONNX conversion
published as Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2, from sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
is licensed under Apache-2.0; Transformers.js (model/lib/transformers.min.js) is
licensed under Apache-2.0; and ONNX Runtime Web
(model/lib/ort-wasm-simd-threaded.jsep.wasm, and the parts of it bundled in
Transformers.js) is licensed under the MIT licence by Microsoft Corporation.

The files in data/ are third-party word lists and word norms and keep their own
licences, which are set out in data/README.md. In brief: data/lists/dale-chall.txt
(from github.com/words/dale-chall) and data/lists/excess_words.csv (from
github.com/berenslab/llm-excess-vocab; Kobak et al. 2025) are MIT-licensed, as are
the copies of them in src/dalechall.txt and src/excess.txt and in index.html. The
four files in data/norms/ are NOT under the MIT licence: the concreteness norms
(Brysbaert, Warriner & Kuperman 2014), the age-of-acquisition norms (Kuperman,
Stadthagen-Gonzalez & Brysbaert 2012) and SUBTLEX-US (Brysbaert & New 2009) are
licensed CC BY-NC-ND 3.0, and the word prevalence norms (Brysbaert, Mandera,
McCormick & Keuleers 2019) are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. They are for
non-commercial use, are loaded only on request, and can be deleted without
affecting the rest of the application.

data/lists/awl.json (the Academic Word List; Coxhead 2000), data/lists/afl.json
(the Academic Formulas List with formula teaching worth; Simpson-Vlach & Ellis
2010) and data/taxonomy/uefap-functions.json (the names of UEFAP's rhetorical
functions; Gillett) hold word strings and numbers only, credited to those
authors. This project claims no copyright in their contents and waives, under
CC0 1.0, any rights it may hold in their arrangement. No permission has been
given by the authors or publishers; see data/README.md. They are fetched only on
request and can be deleted without affecting the rest of the application.

data/phrases/academic-phrases.json is NOT under the MIT licence. It is a JSON
conversion of the phrase table in the Emacs package academic-phrases, Copyright
(C) 2017-2018 Nasser Alshammari, licensed under the GNU General Public License
version 3 or later (text in data/phrases/LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt). The package
states that it is based on Adrian Wallwork's "English for Writing Research
Papers: Useful Phrases" and was made with the permission of Springer Nature and
Adrian Wallwork. The file is kept apart from the application, is fetched only on
request, and can be deleted without affecting the rest of the application.

src/syllables.txt, and the copy of it in index.html, holds syllable counts taken
from the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary, Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon
University, distributed under a BSD 2-clause licence whose full text is in
data/lists/CMUdict-LICENSE.txt. src/jargon.txt and
data/lists/science_common_words_Plaven-Sigray_et_al_2017.csv are from
github.com/wiheto/readabilityinscience (MIT; Plaven-Sigray et al. 2017).

src/akl.txt, data/lists/akl.json and the copy in index.html are the Academic
Keyword List: Paquot, M. (2010). Academic Vocabulary in Learner Writing: From
Extraction to Analysis. London & New York: Continuum, 56-58. The list is
published by the Centre for English Corpus Linguistics, UCLouvain, under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0), not under
the MIT licence above. The entries are unchanged.

src/wordlists.txt, data/lists/words-*.txt and the copy in index.html are the
lists hedges, weasels, fillers and buzzwords from github.com/words, Copyright
(c) 2014 Titus Wormer, MIT licence (text in data/lists/words-LICENSE.txt).
